 Rules are checked top to bottom and the first match wins. Every condition has to match.
 `{app_id}` expands to the original name, which is how one rule covers both browsers.
+
+Rules normally finalize at the first buffered mapping commit. A window that must be identified
+before an earlier empty commit can opt in with `finalize = "identity"`. These rules may only
+use `app_id` and `when.title_contains`, and must precede mapping-time rules for the same app:
+
+```toml
+[[rule]]
+app_id = ["firefox"]
+finalize = "identity"
+when.title_contains = "Picture-in-Picture"
+then.app_id = "{app_id}-pip"
+```
 [rules.example.toml](rules.example.toml) documents every condition.
 
